## 1. Why Cubical Type Theory Carries Relational Physics

Hyperactivity's core paper (`docs/hyperactivity.cub`, Part I) already establishes three structural correspondences with RQM:

1. **Observer-relative facts without a view from nowhere:** An observer $o$ sees only the fiber $\mathsf{Fib}_o(y)$ over its observations, never a global canonical state. Laws are observer-relative statements descending through $o$; warrants refine along observations (`Warrants`, `warrants-refine`).
2. **Information theory at the center (Shannon, Landauer, Wheeler, Rovelli, Church/Turing):** In `lqg/info.cub`, we prove universally that pulling any family of $k$ mutually independent yes/no questions back across an arbitrary channel preserves independence (`qi-data-processing`), forcing the finite capacity bound $2^k \le |S|$ (`rp-postulate1`), while any cubical equivalence (`QiEquiv` / univalence `ua`) transports all $k$ independent bits losslessly in both directions with **zero Landauer erasure** (`qi-equiv-zero-erasure`). Conversely, projecting into a $2^M$-state target necessarily erases any $(M+1)$-st independent bit (`qi-landauer-bottleneck`).
3. **Content-addressed dependency closure:** Every physical assertion carries the exact cryptographic hash of its assumptions and proofs in `store/`. Nothing is claimed without a checked witness.

